# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation Report

## Summary
Vercel Web Analytics has **already been implemented** in this project. No additional changes were required.

## Current Implementation
The project is an HTML-based web application (UMBC Radar), and the Vercel Web Analytics tracking code has been properly integrated into the main HTML file.

### Implementation Details

**File:** `index.html` (lines 13-17)
```html
<!-- Vercel Web Analytics -->
<script>
    window.va = window.va || function () { (window.vaq = window.vaq || []).push(arguments); };
</script>
<script defer src="/_vercel/insights/script.js"></script>
```

## Implementation Verification

✅ **Correct Implementation:** The code follows the official Vercel Web Analytics documentation for HTML sites exactly:
- The `window.va` function is initialized to queue analytics calls
- The tracking script is loaded with `defer` attribute from `/_vercel/insights/script.js`
- The script is placed in the `<head>` section for optimal loading

✅ **Framework Match:** This is an HTML/JavaScript project (not React, Next.js, Vue, etc.), so the plain HTML implementation is the correct approach.

✅ **No Package Required:** As documented, HTML implementations don't need the `@vercel/analytics` npm package.

## Next Steps for the User

To complete the Vercel Web Analytics setup:

1. **Enable Web Analytics in Vercel Dashboard:**
   - Go to the [Vercel dashboard](https://vercel.com/dashboard)
   - Select the `umbc-free-food-radar` project
   - Click the **Analytics** tab
   - Click **Enable** from the dialog

2. **Deploy the Application:**
   - The code is already integrated, so just deploy:
     ```bash
     vercel deploy
     ```

3. **Verify Tracking:**
   - After deployment, visit the site
   - Open browser DevTools → Network tab
   - Look for a request to `/_vercel/insights/view` when pages load
   - This confirms analytics is working

4. **View Analytics Data:**
   - Return to the Vercel dashboard
   - Navigate to Project → Analytics tab
   - Data will appear after users visit the site

## Technical Notes

- **Route Support:** HTML implementation doesn't include automatic route change detection (only available with framework integrations like Next.js, React, Vue, etc.)
- **Privacy Compliant:** Vercel Web Analytics is privacy-focused and doesn't use cookies
- **No Build Required:** Since this is a static HTML site, no build process or dependency installation is needed

## Conclusion

The Vercel Web Analytics implementation is complete and production-ready. The user only needs to enable analytics in the Vercel dashboard and deploy the application to start tracking visitors and page views.
